aws ec2 describe-images `
   --region ap-south-1 `
   --owners amazon `
   --filter "Name=description, Values=Amazon Linux 2023 AMI 2023.10.20260216.1 x86_64 HVM kernel-6.1"
==============================================================================
This command is a precision search using the human-readable Description field rather than the technical Name field. 
It is particularly useful when you have the exact "display name" from the AWS Console and want to find its corresponding AMI ID via the CLI. 

Why use the Description Filter?
Console Matching: The Amazon EC2 Console often displays the Description more prominently than the Name. This command bridges that gap.
Exact Versioning: By specifying 2023.10.20260216.1, you are ensuring that your script uses a specific, immutable version of the OS, 
which is critical for production stability. Amazon Linux 2023 AMI Versions
Regional Accuracy: Adding --region ap-south-1 ensures you are looking at the Mumbai inventory, as AMI IDs change across regions even if the description is the same.
